        "original_id": "71763fdb-a9e3-572f-94d0-85baa859383f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dave Peverett, Jimi Hendrix, Charlie Huhn, Bryan Bassett\n- Bands: Foghat, Savoy Brown\n- Works: Family Joules\n- Roles: singer, musician, guitarist, songwriter, lead vocalist, rhythm guitarist\n\nFacts:\n- Jimi Hendrix was born Johnny Allen Hendrix on November 27, 1942, and he became an American rock guitarist, singer, and songwriter.\n- Dave Peverett was born on April 16, 1943, and he was an English singer and musician also known as Lonesome Dave.\n- Dave Peverett served in Savoy Brown before he founded the rock band Foghat.\n- Dave Peverett was the original lead vocalist and rhythm guitarist of Foghat.\n- Jimi Hendrix died on September 18, 1970.\n- Family Joules was the first album by Foghat without founding member Dave Peverett.\n- Family Joules was the first Foghat album to feature singer-guitarist Charlie Huhn and guitarist Bryan Bassett.\n- Dave Peverett died on February 7, 2000.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
